  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">Add the polynomial functions. Evaluate the sum for each given value.</para>
<para id="para-00002">\(z(x) = 8x^2 + 4x - 6\)          \(w(x) = -5x^2 + 2x + 3\)</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00003">\( (z + w)(x) = \) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00005">\((z + w)(x) = 3x^2 + 6x - 3\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00006">\( (z + w)(6) = \) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00008">\((z + w)(6) = 141\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    <para id="para-00009">\((z + w)(-9) = \) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00011">\((z + w)(-9) = 186\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00004">
  <problem id="prob-00004">
    <para id="para-00012">\((z + w)(0)\) = ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00004">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00014">\((z + w)(0) = -3\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para id="para-00015">Subtract the polynomial functions. Evaluate the sum for each given value.</para>
<para id="para-00016">\(m(x) = -6x^2 + 2x - 8\)          \(n(x) = -x^2 - 7x - 6\)</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00005">
  <problem id="prob-00005">
    <para id="para-00017">\((m - n)(x) =\) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00005">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00019">\((m - n)(x) = -5x^2 + 9x - 2\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00006">
  <problem id="prob-00006">
    <para id="para-00020">\((m - n)(-2) =\) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00006">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00021">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00022">\((m - n)(-2) = -40\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00007">
  <problem id="prob-00007">
    <para id="para-00023">\( (m - n)(0) =\) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00007">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00024">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00025">\((m - n)(0) = -2\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00008">
  <problem id="prob-00008">
    <para id="para-00026">\((m - n)(4) =\) ___________</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00008">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00027">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00028">\((m - n)(4) = -46\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00009">
  <problem id="prob-00009">
    <para id="para-00029">What is a good way to check that you found the correct sum or difference when adding or subtracting polynomial functions?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00009">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00030">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00031">Substitute a value for \(x\) into the individual polynomial functions. Add or subtract the results. The answer should be equal to the value you find when you substitute it into the sum or difference of the polynomial functions.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
<section id="sect-00002">
<title>Video: Combining and Evaluating Polynomial Functions</title>
<para id="para-00032">Watch the following video to learn more about how to add and subtract polynomial functions and evaluate them at a given value:</para>
<media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text"><iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/eaecc03382b9de51eb04d6d681ab65c784d6e188"/></media></section>

<note class="self-check" id="note-00001"><para id="para-00033">For functions \(f(x)=5x^2-4x-1\) and \(g(x)=x^2+3x+8\), find:</para>
  <para id="para-00034">        \((f+g)(x) =\) _______</para>
  <para id="para-00035">        \((f+g)(5) =\) _______</para></note>

  <section id="sect-00003"><title>Additional Resources</title>
    <section id="sect-00004"><title> Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>
      <para id="para-00036">Just as polynomials can be added and subtracted, polynomial functions can also be added and subtracted.</para>
      
      <note id="note-00002">
        <para id="para-00037"><emphasis>For functions \(f(x)\) and \(g(x)\),</emphasis></para>
        
        <list id="list-00001">
          <item>\((f + g)(x) = f(x) + g(x)\)</item>
          <item>\((f - g)(x) = f(x) - g(x)\)</item>
        </list>
      </note>
      
      <para id="para-00038">Let’s look at some examples.</para>
      <para id="para-00039">For the functions \(f(x) = 3x^2-5x+7\) and \(g(x) = x^2-4x-3\), find:</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
        <item>\((f+g)(x)\)</item>
        <item>\(
          (f+g)(3)
          \)</item>
        <item>\(
          (f-g)(x)
          \)</item>
        <item>\(
          (f-g)(-2)
          \)</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00040">The following is a step-by-step breakdown.
     </para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
        <item>(\(f+g)(x)=f(x)+g(x)\)</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00041"><emphasis>Step 1 - 
       </emphasis> Substitute</para>
      <para id="para-00042">\(f(x)={\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7}\) and \(g(x)={\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3}\).
        \((f+g)(x)=({\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7})+{\style{color:blue}(}{\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3}{\style{color:blue})}\)</para>
      <para id="para-00043"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Rewrite without the parentheses.</para>
      <para id="para-00044"> \((f+g)(x)=3x^2-5x+7-x^2-4x-3\)</para>
      <para id="para-00045"><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Put like terms together.</para>
      <para id="para-00046"> \((f+g)(x)=3x^2+x^2-5x-4x+7-3\)</para>
      <para id="para-00047"><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Combine like terms.</para>
      <para id="para-00048"> \((f+g)(x)=4x^2-9x+4\)</para>
      <para id="para-00049">In part (a), we found \((f+g)(x)\), and now are asked to find \((f+g)(3)\).</para>
      
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00004">
        <item>\((f+g)(x)=4x^2-9x+4\)</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00050"><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> To find \((f+g)(3)\), substitute \(x=3\).</para>
      <para id="para-00051"> \((f+g)(3)=4(3)^2-9 \cdot 3+4\)</para>
      <para id="para-00052"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Simplify.</para>
      <para id="para-00053"> \((f+g)(3)=4 \cdot 9-9 \cdot 3+ 4\)
        \((f+g)(3)=36-27+4\)
        \((f+g)(3)=13\)</para>
      <para id="para-00054">Notice that we could have found \((f+g)(3)\) by first finding the values of \(f(3)\) and \(g(3)\) separately and then adding the results.</para>
      <para id="para-00055"><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Find \(f (3)\).</para>
      <para id="para-00056"> \(f(x)=3x^2-5x+7\)
        \( f({\style{color:red}3})=3({\style{color:red}3})^2-5({\style{color:red}3})+7\)
        \(f(3)=19\)</para>
      <para id="para-00057"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Find \(g(3)\).</para>
      <para id="para-00058"> \(g(x)=x^2-4x-3\)
        \(g(3)=-6\)</para>
      <para id="para-00059"><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Find \((f+g)(3)\).</para>
      <para id="para-00060"> \((f+g)(x)=f(x)+g(x)\)
        \((f+g)(3)=f(3)+g(3)\)</para>
      <para id="para-00061"><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Substitute \(f(3)={\style{color:red}1}{\style{color:red}9}\) and \(g(3)= {\style{color:blue}-}{\style{color:blue}6}\).</para>
      <para id="para-00062"> \((f+g)(3)=19+(-6)\)
        \((f+g)(3)=13\)</para>
      
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00005">
        <item>\((f-g)(x)=f(x)-g(x)\)</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00063"><emphasis>Step 1 - 
       </emphasis> Substitute</para>
      <para id="para-00064">\(f(x)={\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7}\) and \(g(x)= {\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3}\).
        \((f-g)(x)=( {\style{color:red}3}{\style{color:red}x}^{\style{color:red}2}\;{\style{color:red}-}\;{\style{color:red}5}{\style{color:red}x}\;{\style{color:red}+}\;{\style{color:red}7})-({\style{color:blue}x}^{\style{color:blue}2}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}4}{\style{color:blue}x}\;{\style{color:blue}-}\;{\style{color:blue}3})\)</para>
      <para id="para-00065"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Rewrite without the parentheses.</para>
      <para id="para-00066"> \((f-g)(x)=3x^2-5x+7-x^2+4x+3\)</para>
      <para id="para-00067"><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Put like terms together.</para>
      <para id="para-00068"> \((f-g)(x)=3x^2-x^2-5x+4x+7+3\)</para>
      <para id="para-00069"><emphasis>Step 4 - 
       </emphasis> Combine like terms.</para>
      <para id="para-00070"> \((f-g)(x)=2x^2-x+10\)</para>
      
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00006">
        <item>\((f-g)(x)=2x^2-x+10\)</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00071"><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> To find \((f-g)(-2)\), substitute \(x={\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2}\).</para>
      <para id="para-00072"> \((f-g)( {\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})=2({\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})^2-({\style{color:red}-}{\style{color:red}2})+10\)</para>
      <para id="para-00073"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Simplify.</para>
      <para id="para-00074"> \((f-g)(-2)=2 \cdot 5-(-2)+10\)
        \((f-g)(-2)=20\)</para>
      <note id="note-00003">
      <title> Try It: Adding and Subtracting Polynomial Functions</title>
      
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          
          <para id="para-00075">For functions \(f(x)=2x^2-4x+3\) and \(g(x)=x^2-2x-6\), find:</para>
          
          <para id="para-00076">\((f+g)(x)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00077">\((f+g)(3)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00078">\((f-g)(x)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00079">\((f-g)(-2)\)</para>
          <para id="para-00080">Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        
        </problem><solution id="sol-00010">
        <para id="para-00081">Here is how to add and subtract the polynomial functions:</para>
        
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00007">
          <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f+g)(x)&amp;=&amp;(2x^2-4x+3)+(x^2-2x-6)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^2-4x+3+x^2-2x-6\\&amp;=&amp;3x^2-6x-3\end{array}\)
            
         </item>
          <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f+g)(3)&amp;=&amp;3(3)^2-6(3)-3\\&amp;=&amp;3(9)-6(3)-3\\&amp;=&amp;27-18-3\\&amp;=&amp;6\end{array}\)
         </item>
          <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f-g)(x)&amp;=&amp;(2x^2-4x+3)-(x^2-2x-6)\\&amp;=&amp;2x^2-4x+3-x^2+2x+6\\&amp;=&amp;x^2-2x+9\;\end{array}\)
            
         </item>
          <item>\(\begin{array}{rcl}(f-g)(-2)&amp;=&amp;(-2)^2-2(-2)+9\;\\&amp;=&amp;(4)+4+9\;\\&amp;=&amp;17\;\end{array}\)</item>
        </list>
      
      </solution></exercise></note>
      </section>
  </section>


